{
  "dom_id": "step-q94978",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The diastolic blood pressure of a group of people is normally distributed with a mean of $85\\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}$ and a standard deviation of $14\\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected person from the group has a diastolic blood pressure greater than $77\\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}$ and less than $86\\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}?$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.6\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2546\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2514\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2483\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.5\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2877\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2843\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2810\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3228\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3192\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3156\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4364\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4325\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4286\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.0\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5239\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5279\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5319\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5636\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5675\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5714\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the diastolic blood pressure of the selected person. Then we have $X∼N(85,{14}^{2}).$\n\nWe want to find $P(77<X<86).$ First, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(77<X<86) & =P(\\frac{77-85}{14}<Z<\\frac{86-85}{14}) \\\\  & =P(-0.57<Z<0.07)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.57<Z<0.07) & =P(Z<0.07)-P(Z\\le -0.57) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.07)-P(Z\\le -0.57) \\\\  & =Φ(0.07)-Φ(-0.57)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.07) & =0.5279 \\\\ Φ(-0.57) & =0.2843\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.57<Z<0.07) & =Φ(0.07)-Φ(-0.57) \\\\  & =0.5279-0.2843 \\\\  & =0.2436.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the randomly selected person from the group has a diastolic blood pressure greater than $77\\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}$ and less than $86\\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}$ is approximately $0.24.$",
